அவர் தான் Delegate (பிரதிநிதி).

What is Delegate
•	It is a type-safe function pointer.
•	A delegate holds the reference of a method and then calls the method for execution
•	In c#, we can call the method in 2 ways
  1.	By using the instance of the class, if it is a non-static method
  2.	By using the name of the class if it is a static method
  3.	Here additionally, using delegate we can call the method
•	To call a method by using a delegate we have 3 steps
1.	Define a Delegate
<modifier> delegate void | type <name>(<parameter>);
Example Method signature- public void AddNums(int a, int b)
Example Delegate definition(signature) - public delegate void AddDelegate(int a, int b);
Note – method name and delegate name will not be same
2 important points to remember while defining a delegate
1. The return type of the delegate should exactly match with the return type of the method
2. The parameter type of the delegate should exactly be same type of parameter of the method
Example Method Signature - public static string SayHello(string name)
Example delegate definition(signature) - public delegate string SayDelegate(string name);
Remember a delegate is a type like class, structure, interface all these are user-defined types, delegate also user-defined type
The main difference between the structure and class is Class is a reference type meanwhile structure is a value type, same way a delegate is also a reference type
In c#, we generally define type(class, interface) under namespaces
Why, types are going to be defined under namespaces and namespaces is a logical container of types 
2.	Instantiating a delegate
•	In the process of instantiation, we will create a instance of a delegate, why, delegate is a reference type and at the time of instantiating a delegate you require to pass the method as a parameter to the delegate
•	Instantiating is a process of creating a instance of the delegate and in the process, you require to pass the method as a parameter to the delegate constructor
•	AddDelegate ad = new AddDelegate(p.AddNums);
SayDelegate sd = new SayDelegate(Program.sayHello);

3.	Call the Delegate
•	Call the delegate by passing required parameter values, so that internally the method which is bound with the delegate gets executed.
